From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean O'Hollaren <sean.ohollaren@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:31:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FM-1: the large message line in the game's own font

The plain capitals drawn for it were readable but not the game's. The line is now written in the
font the game uses for its own messages (the STCFN patches), a row at a time through draw_vpatch
into a row of its own, each of the font's pixels as 2 x 2 on the panel, straight onto the picture
with no band behind it, from the top left as the game's messages are. fm1_osd.h breaks a message
into up to three lines by the letters' widths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fm1/fm1_osd.h   | 163 ++++++++++----------------------------------
 src/fm1/fm1_video.c |  69 +++++++++++++++++--
 src/fm1/fm1_web.c   |   4 ++
 3 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 131 deletions(-)

